From: shuxueshuxue <98064968+shuxueshuxue@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 01:50:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gugu: forward forkSession for Claude sessions

Why: newSession() receives `_meta.claudeCode.options.forkSession` but drops
it, so Gugu's runtime fork (resume + fork, nothing written to disk) silently
degrades into a plain resume of the parent session. ACP's standard
session/fork is not a substitute: it forks the transcript on disk and does
not create a live session.

A fork is a new session: like any new session it runs under the id this
bridge minted for it (`options.sessionId`), which Claude honours with
--resume + --fork-session (checked with Claude 2.1.282: system/init reports
exactly that id, and persistSession: false still writes nothing). An earlier
revision of this patch left the id to Claude and adopted
`initializationResult.session_id` instead; Claude does not report one there,
so the bridge kept a random id while every SDK message carried Claude's own
child id, and the updates keyed by `message.session_id` (rate limits,
compaction, tool progress) named a session no client knew (gugu#6552).

Upstream: agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp#1108 forwards forkSession;
this patch keeps that part and drops its session-id change.

Drop when: forkSession forwarding is in the upstream tag this fork is
rebased on.
---
